  "title": "Struck by a Whale",
  "subtitle": "The Essex Disaster and the True Story Behind Moby-Dick",
  "authorDisplayName": "Liszt Think",
  "description": "On November 20, 1820, a sperm whale rammed and sank the Nantucket whaleship Essex in the remote Pacific. Twenty men took to three open whaleboats, choosing a perilous eastward course over feared cannibal islands. What followed was ninety days of starvation, separation, and the drawing of lots that forced survivors to consume their dead. This narrative history reconstructs the catastrophe through conflicting accounts by first mate Owen Chase and cabin boy Thomas Nickerson, verified against ship registers, insurance records, and rescue logs. Where memories diverge, the documentary record speaks. From the moment of impact to the silent return to Nantucket and Herman Melville’s marginal annotations, every detail is anchored in primary evidence. Struck by a Whale strips away myth to reveal the grueling arithmetic of survival at sea, offering a definitive account of the tragedy that shaped American literature.",
