  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This panoramic reconstruction achieves its highest standard by anchoring the Essex disaster in a concrete, recurring thesis—the 'ledger mentality'—which powerfully explains decisions from outfitting to the final, desperate lot-drawing. The narrative drive is compelling, built on dated physical particulars that grant the ordeal a stark immediacy, such as the deck tilting under a crewman's boots. However, the book's immersive power is partially undone in its final section, where the voice drifts from scene-stamped narration into retrospective summary and literary analysis, losing the gripping mo",
